msgid "How this plugin works"
msgstr ""

msgid "The two halves"
msgstr ""

msgid "Your supplier runs \"Woo Wholesale Pro\" and maintains the products there. This shop runs \"Woo Wholesale Partner\" and fetches them. Both plugins belong to the same release and should always be updated together."
msgstr ""

msgid "Getting started"
msgstr ""

msgid "Enter the address of the supplier shop and your partner key under \"Supplier\", then use \"Test connection\"."
msgstr ""

msgid "Set your markup under \"Prices\" - you can change it later at any time."
msgstr ""

msgid "Run the first sync under \"Sync\". New products are created as drafts, so you can check them first."
msgstr ""

msgid "Check under \"Images\" whether anything is still missing, and publish the products."
msgstr ""

msgid "How your price is calculated"
msgstr ""

msgid "Sales price = purchase price × (1 + markup ÷ 100), then rounded the way you chose. The markup of the most specific category of a product wins; if no category has one, the standard markup is used."
msgstr ""

msgid "A price you type into a product by hand is replaced the next time prices are recalculated. If you want to keep a special price for one article, use a sale price - a sale price below the calculated price is left alone."
msgstr ""

msgid "Why some fields cannot be edited"
msgstr ""

msgid "Your supplier decides which product data it maintains. Those fields are shown as locked, and if something changes them anyway - a bulk edit, an import, another plugin through the REST API - the supplier value is written back when the product is saved. Your prices, your stock and your own products are not affected."
msgstr ""

msgid "Images are only downloaded from the supplier shop, never from any other address, and only if they really are images. An image that is too large or unreachable is retried later instead of stopping the sync."
msgstr ""

msgid "If something goes wrong"
msgstr ""

msgid "\"Unknown or revoked partner key\": ask your supplier for a new key, keys can be replaced at any time."
msgstr ""

msgid "No answer on the partner route: the supplier shop needs Woo Wholesale Pro 1.1.0 or newer."
msgstr ""

msgid "A sync that stops in the middle can simply be started again; it continues where it makes sense and never creates a product twice."
msgstr ""

msgid "Image check"
msgstr ""

msgid "A sync never fails because of an image. Whatever could not be fetched stays in a queue, is retried in the background with a growing delay, and is picked up here. The check also walks through the products that are already here and compares what should be there against what really is - so an image that was deleted later, or never arrived, is fetched again."
msgstr ""

